ntempt  of Congress charge was one of the three  things in the articles of impeachment  against Richard Nixon back in 1974 I  told you last week that Trump 2019 is  looking more  more like Nixon 1974 and yesterday on  the show I did a story outlining how the  difference between 2019 and 1974 isn't  that what Nixon did is worse than what  Trump has done it's that Republicans in  the 70s drew the line at abuses of power  of this level even by people in their  party Republicans in 2019 on the other  hand don't care about that they have no  such line so that is why this is so  interesting but to get back to the  contempt it self contempt of Congress  against the sitting Attorney General is  unlikely to ever actually be carried  fully out because when think - what  libertarians always talk about they say  the government is an initiator of force  because eventually men with guns will  come for you doesn't sound like taxation  is uh some kind of slavery under duress  well if you don't pay your taxes  eventually men with guns show up that  actually is a relevant thing to think  about when it comes to contempt of  Congress against William bar because if  the House Committee votes to hold Barr  in contempt and then the full house  votes to hold Barr in contempt and  everything else that has to follow from  that and happen to hold Barr in contempt  does happen at some point somebody has  to physically detain William Barr is the  house sergeant at arms going to  physically detain the Attorney General  very difficult to imagine that that's  going to happen is a court a court which  is of course part of the Justice  Department that William bar himself  oversees going to physically detain  William bar hard to imagine that that's  going to happen so the actual holding in  contempt of the Attorney General is more  symbolic than anything but the reason  why it matters is that this is another  one of these striking similarities to  Richard Nixon in 1974 and it is  political theater I 